Parents of babies from the newborn stage to 10 months weigh crying, sleep training and responsiveness against severe sleep deprivation. They fear brain or nervous-system damage, abandonment or loss of trust, while also questioning how exhaustion affects daytime parenting and the family's wellbeing. Attempts include gentle methods, bedsharing, contact sleep and repeated transfers; some describe changes of position or later improvement.

- "I’m worried about that hurting his little brain by raising his cortisol levels and teaching him that he can’t trust that I’ll be there for him. However at this point I don’t have much of an option. I think I may try this. The only issue is that our only bathroom is in his room lol. My boyfriend and I will just have to make sure that we are ready for bed and our bladders are empty. I feel like he is going to cry for hours until falling asleep. How long is too long to let him cry?" [sr038-0014]
